ad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8525794744491577, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(808.7885691666669), np.float64(1240.6834125)), (np.float64(808.7885691666669), np.float64(1279.4750791666663)), (np.float64(1577.4810791015625), np.float64(1279.4750791666663)), (np.float64(1577.4810791015625), np.float64(1240.6834125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2894, 'layout_height': 4094}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T16:05:13', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 1, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'parent_id': '0e00572bd5a1d90e1f7c6e9bdd19e988', 'category': 'ListItem', 'element_id': '0491add8bc8e5908e3b62599e9c5a65a'}, page_content='* Correspondence: irina.radeva@iict.bas.bg'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9457063674926758, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(808.787293465278), np.float64(1357.298541666667)), (np.float64(808.787293465278), np.float64(2285.6866666666674)), (np.float64(2730.4069693541687), np.float64(2285.6866666666674)), (np.float64(2730.4069693541687), np.float64(1357.298541666667))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2894, 'layout_height': 4094}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T16:05:13', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 1, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'parent_id': '0e00572bd5a1d90e1f7c6e9bdd19e988', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'f7e7a1f6dfa50084b4e09d6fd44f8015'}, page_content='Abstract: The purpose of this paper is to explore the implementation of retrieval-augmented gener- ation (RAG) technology with open-source large language models (LLMs). A dedicated web-based application, PaSSER, was developed, integrating RAG with Mistral:7b, Llama2:7b, and Orca2:7b models. Various software instruments were used in the application’s development. PaSSER employs a set of evaluation metrics, including METEOR, ROUGE, BLEU, perplexity, cosine similarity, Pear- son correlation, and F1 score, to assess LLMs’ performance, particularly within the smart agriculture domain. The paper presents the results and analyses of two tests. One test assessed the performance of LLMs across diﬀerent hardware conﬁgurations, while the other determined which model deliv- ered the most accurate and contextually relevant responses within RAG. The paper discusses the integration of blockchain with LLMs to manage and store assessment results within a blockchain environment. The tests revealed that GPUs are essential for fast text generation, even for 7b models. Orca2:7b on Mac M1 was the fastest, and Mistral:7b had superior performance on the 446 question– answer dataset. The discussion is on technical and hardware considerations aﬀecting LLMs’ perfor- mance. The conclusion outlines future developments in leveraging other LLMs, ﬁne-tuning ap- proaches, and further integration with blockchain and IPFS.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.892503023147583, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(170.92874145507812), np.float64(2329.082275390625)), (np.float64(170.92874145507812), np.float64(2714.3146916666656)), (np.float64(729.4055813333333), np.float64(2714.3146916666656)), (np.float64(729.4055813333333), np.float64(2329.082275390625))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2894, 'layout_height': 4094}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T16:05:13', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 1, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad7