1007392474ce67f43c098'}, page_content='2. Web Application Development and Implementation'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8943825960159302, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(808.7928333333336), np.float64(2485.460693359375)), (np.float64(808.7928333333336), np.float64(2602.034341666664)), (np.float64(2731.3107499999996), np.float64(2602.034341666664)), (np.float64(2731.3107499999996), np.float64(2485.460693359375))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2894, 'layout_height': 4094}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T16:05:13', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 3, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'parent_id': '388dcb9235e1007392474ce67f43c098', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '1d1f18ba1ca3064779baaa0439dfc8af'}, page_content='This section describes the development, implementation, and features of the PaSSER Web App, which henceforward will be referred to as the PaSSER App.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.949621856212616, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(808.7928333333331), np.float64(2615.453487499997)), (np.float64(808.7928333333331), np.float64(3287.1414041666635)), (np.float64(2731.4422624999997), np.float64(3287.1414041666635)), (np.float64(2731.4422624999997), np.float64(2615.453487499997))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2894, 'layout_height': 4094}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T16:05:13', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 3, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'parent_id': '388dcb9235e1007392474ce67f43c098', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'e87a05e7e0071c77de377c52c76411ca'}, page_content='The PaSSER App is a complementary project to the Smart crop production data ex- change (SCPDx) platform, described in detail in [10,11]. The platform aims to support the integration of exchanging information and data acquired or generated as a result of the use of diﬀerent technologies in smart agriculture. An underlying blockchain and distrib- uted ﬁle system, eosio blockchain and InterPlanetary ﬁle system (IPFS), were selected [12]. The networks were deployed as private, permissionless. Later, in 2022, due to the hard fork, eosio blockchain was renamed to Antelope.io [13], which forced the migration of the blockchain network. The development of the SCPDx platform was preceded by a number of studies related to the choice of blockchain platform [14], blockchain-enabled supply- chain modelling for a smart crop production framework [15], and blockchain oracles in- tegration [16].'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9247817993164062, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(808.7928333333331), np.float64(3300.847929166664)), (np.float64(808.7928333333331), np.float64(3474.093729166664)), (np.float64(2731.4276500000014), np.float64(3474.093729166664)), (np.float64(2731.4276500000014), np.float64(3300.847929166664))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2894, 'layout_height': 4094}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T16:05:13', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 3, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'parent_id': '388dcb9235e1007392474ce67f43c098', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'd2dec73afff3e3d7dc34aae4e876123f'}, page_content='The framework outlined in Figure 1 represents the PaSSER App’s core infrastructure, the server side, the application itself, and the integration with the blockchain and IPFS of the SCPDx platform infrastructure.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9434542059898376, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(808.7916666666664), np.float64(3487.8002541666638)), (np.float64(808.7916666666664), np.float64(3787.88037109375)), (np.float64(2731.3290666666653), np.float64(3787.88037109375)), (np.float64(2731.3290666666653), np.float64(3487.8002541666638))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2894, 'layout_height': 4094}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T16:05:13', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 3, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'parent_id': '388dcb9235e1007392474ce67f43c098', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '21a2013440b6d1b9abdc0f67b42b37f8'}, page_content='There are diﬀerent ways and techniques to work with LLMs and the RAG technology (Python scripts, desktop or web apps), but from a user’s perspective, it is most convenient to use a web interface as it is independent of software platforms, where access to external resources is implemented through APIs. This is why the PaSSER App was developed as a web application.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8619546890258789, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(2579.511474609375), np.float64(256.60992431640625)), (np.float64(2579.511474609375), np.float64(300.75469970703125)), (np.float64(2728.608866666666), np.float64(300.75469970703125)), (np.float64(2728.608866666666), np.float64(256.60992431640625))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2894, 'layout_height': 4094}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T16:05:13', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 3, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'category': 'Header', 'element_id': '22ba81dd466435fbe38286f28d3b1241'}, page_content='3 of 31'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8978127837181091, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(174.68499755859375), np.float64(260.9737083333338)), (np.float64(174.68499755859375), np.float64(299.765375)), (np.float64(602.0708561875), np.float64(299.765375)), (np.float64(602.0708561875), np.float64(260.9737083333338))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2894, 'layout_height': 4094}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T16:05:13', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 4, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'category': 'Header', 'element_id': '6693ceb1baed378a217627de62adb949'}, page_content='Electronics 2024, 13, 1361'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9450053572654724, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(806.1951904296875), np.float64(453.446044921875)), (np.float64(806.1951904296875), np.float64(755.5306499999989)), (np.float64(2731.4003733333334), np.float64(755.5306499999989)), (np.float64(2731.4003733333334), np.float64(453.446044921875))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2894, 'layout_height': 4094}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T16:05:13', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 4, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'parent_id': '6693ceb1baed378a217627de62adb949', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'c96b7a10020bbd0640793d493a8a0907'}, page_content='The PaSSER App communicates with Ollama [17], ChromaDB [18], Python scripts, Antelope blockchain, and IPFS through their respective APIs. Currently, the IPFS network is not utilized within the framework; however, future enhancements aim to incorporate it to enable storage and content distribution, which will support the ﬁne-tuning processes of LLMs.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.7477515935897827, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(800.011474609375), np.float64(1644.0068749999998)), (np.float64(800.011474609375), np.float64(1687.7568749999998)), (np.float64(1485.2778163124997), np.float64(1687.7568749999998)), (np.float64(1485.2778163124997), np.float64(1644.0068749999998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2894, 'layout_height': 4094}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T16:05:13', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 4, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'category': 'FigureCaption', 'element_id': '694479760682c67d7b74e15c8ba848ad'}, page_content='Figure 1. PaSSER App framework.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9470850229263306, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(799.79345703125), np.float64(1757.371826171875)), (np.float64(799.79345703125), np.float64(2119.9513708333334)), (np.float64(2731.3263444444456), np.float64(2119.9513708333334)), (np.float64(2731.3263444444456), np.float64(1757.371826171875))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2894, 'layout_height': 4094}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T16:05:13', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 4, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'eaf115f3a844291d7f261128c984de09'}, page_content='The PaSSER App is developed in JavaScript, leveraging the PrimeReact library [19] for its user interface components. To facilitate interaction with the Antelope blockchain network, it employs the WharfKit library [20]. The LangChain library [21] is integrated for engagement with RAG and LLMs. The application is hosted on an Apache web server, enabling communication between the PaSSER App, the LLMs, and the SCPDx infrastruc- ture.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.945600152015686, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(805.8680419921875), np.float64(2133.079345703125)), (np.float64(805.8680419921875), np.float64(2493.5735125)), (np.float64(2731.355557777778), np.float64(2493.5735125)), (np.float64(2731.355557777778), np.float64(2133.079345703125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2894, 'layout_height': 4094}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T16:05:13', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 4, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'a4db87b845de412390ac0340c0659c20'}, page_content='The server component of the PaSSER App includes a vector database, LLM API, and a score evaluation API. Ollama’s API supports diﬀerent operating systems (UBUNTU, Windows, and macOS) and is used as an interface with diﬀerent LLMs. This API grants users the ﬂexibility to manage and interact with diﬀerent open-source LLMs. Speciﬁcally, Ollama is deployed on an Ubuntu server equipped with 128 GB RAM, not utilizing a GPU, and also conﬁgured locally on a Mac Mini M1 with 16 GB RAM and a 10-core GPU.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9517019987106323, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(808.7871399999998), np.float64(2507.2800374999997)), (np.float64(808.7871399999998), np.float64(3054.4304875000007)), (np.float64(2731.4334599999997), np.float64(3054.4304875000007)), (np.float64(2731.4334599999997), np.float64(2507.2800374999997))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2894, 'layout_height': 4094}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T16:05:13', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 4, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '86406fb3cabebc9e687d2505553a3596'}, page_content='ChromaDB is used to work with vector databases. ChromaDB is an open-source vec- tor database for applications that utilize large language models (LLMs). It supports mul- tiple programming languages such as Python, JavaScript, Ruby, Java, Go, and others. The database is licensed under the Apache 2.0 license. ChromaDB architecture is suited for applications that require semantic search capabilities. An embedding refers to the trans- formation of text, images, or audio into a vector of numbers, which represents the essence of the content in a way that can be processed and understood by machine learning models. In this implementation, ChromaDB was installed on a macOS-based server and locally on a Mac Mini M1 16 GB RAM 10 GPU.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9471215605735779, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(808.7871399999999), np.float64(3067.8447625000003)), (np.float64(808.7871399999999), np.float64(3490.642822265625)), (np.float64(2731.628215555559), np.float64(3490.642822265625)), (np.float64(2731.628215555559), np.float64(3067.8447625000003))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2894, 'layout_height': 4094}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T16:05:13', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 4, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '2fcfc804046cd2bbb6afb705cf699bf6'}, page_content='Two Python scripts are developed: one for computing various evaluation metrics us- ing libraries such as NLTK [22], torch [23], numpy [24], rouge [25], transformers [26], and scipy [27], and the other for logging model performance data, both using the Pyntelope library [28] for blockchain interactions. These scripts are operational on an Ubuntu server and are accessible via GitHub [9], facilitating the analysis and the recording of perfor- mance metrics within a blockchain framework to ensure data integrity and reproducibility of results.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.5377070903778076, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(807.2613525390625), np.float64(3562.497370833334)), (np.float64(807.2613525390625), np.float64(3611.205704166667)), (np.float64(1258.4874555555557), np.float64(3611.205704166667)), (np.float64(1258.4874555555557), np.float64(3562.497370833334))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2894, 'layout_height': 4094}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T16:05:13', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 4, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000g