PDX Infrastructure\n- **Title**: SCPDX INFRASTRUCTURE\n- **Components**:\n  - **Antelope blockchain**: Represented by a black square with a white logo.\n  - **IPFS**: Represented by a blue and white cube, which stands for InterPlanetary File System.\n\n### Arrows and Connections:\n- Arrows indicate the flow of data or communication between the components:\n  - From the Local or Server-Based Installation to the Passer Web App.\n  - From the Passer Web App to the SCPDX Infrastructure.\n\n### Overall Structure:\nThe diagram shows a flow from a local or server-based setup, through a web application, and into an infrastructure that includes blockchain and file system technologies. The integration of various tools and services is highlighted to show how they work together in this system."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(807.3333333333334), np.float64(1325.3333333333333)), (np.float64(807.3333333333334), np.float64(2585.3333333333326)), (np.float64(2613.333333333333), np.float64(2585.3333333333326)), (np.float64(2613.333333333333), np.float64(1325.3333333333333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2894, 'layout_height': 4094}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T16:05:13', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 6, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-6-5.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': '120a82794ea21c6ba9ebb37aa002e6b8', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-6-5.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-6-5.jpg\nThe image is a detailed flowchart or menu structure for a system related to creating and managing vector stores, conducting tests, and configuring settings. Here\'s a breakdown of the elements:\n\n### Top Section: "CREATE VECTORSTORE"\n- **From text**: This option allows users to create a vector store from text data.\n- **From pdf**: This option allows users to create a vector store from PDF files.\n- **From web**: This option allows users to create a vector store from web content.\n- **Vectorstore name**: A field where the user can input the name of the vector store.\n- **Upload files**: A field where users can upload files to the vector store.\n- **URL**: A field where users can input a URL to fetch data for the vector store.\n\n### Middle Section: "CHAT"\n- **Chat with LLM**: This option allows users to chat with a Large Language Model (LLM).\n- **RAG Q&A with LLM**: This option allows users to conduct a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) Q&A session with an LLM.\n- **Select Vectorstore**: A button to select the vector store for the chat or RAG Q&A session.\n- **Chat**: A button to initiate the chat or RAG Q&A session.\n\n### Section: "TESTS"\n- **Q&A dataset**: This option allows users to work with a Q&A dataset.\n- **RAG Q&A score test**: This option allows users to conduct a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) Q&A score test.\n- **Show test results**: This option allows users to view the results of the tests.\n- **Q&A time LLM test**: This option allows users to conduct a Q&A time test with an LLM.\n- **Show time test results**: This option allows users to view the results of the time tests.\n- **Prompt**: A field where users can input a prompt for the test.\n- **Referent answers file selection**: A button to select a file containing referent answers.\n- **Test name**: A field where users can input the name of the test.\n- **Select performed tests**: A button to select the tests that have been performed.\n- **Test results**: A field where the results of the tests are displayed.\n- **Export to xlsx**: A button to export the test results to an Excel file.\n\n### Bottom Section: "CONFIGURATION"\n- **Select Ollama path**: A button to select the path to the Ollama server.\n- **Select model**: A button to select a model for the system.\n- **Select ChromaDB**: A button to select a ChromaDB instance.\n- **Temperature**: A field where users can input the temperature for the LLM.\n\n### Bottom Section: "MANAGE DB"\n- **Name**: A field where users can input the name of the database.\n- **id**: A field where users can input the ID of the database.\n- **Delete**: A button to delete the database.\n- **DB info**: A button to view information about the database.\n\n### Bottom Section: "ANCHOR LOGIN"\n- This section likely pertains to user authentication or login functionality.\n\nThe flowchart uses different colors to differentiate between different types of actions and fields, such as red for buttons, blue for fields, and green for additional options.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(807.3333333333334), np.float64(443.333333333333)), (np.float64(807.3333333333334), np.float64(1177.1666666666665)), (np.float64(2685.6666666666665), np.float64(1177.1666666666665)), (np.float64(2685.6666666666665), np.float64(443.333333333333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2894, 'layout_height': 4094}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T16:05:13', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 7, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-7-6.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': '960a7ab97c1ee7aa7b1a21be9e5d7587', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-7-6.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-7-6.jpg\nThe image is a flowchart that illustrates a process for handling content sources, such as PDF files, TXT files, and web page content. The flowchart is divided into several stages, each represented by a box with text and some additional elements like icons or labels.\n\n1. **Content Sources**: This stage includes three types of content sources: PDF files, TXT files, and web page content. These are represented by separate boxes with the respective labels.\n\n2. **Splitting**: This stage involves the process of splitting the content into smaller chunks. The box is labeled "Splitting" and includes an icon of a parrot and a chain, which might symbolize the process of breaking down content into manageable parts. The tool used for this step is mentioned as "LangChain."\n\n3. **Embedding**: This stage involves the creation of embeddings for the content chunks. The box is labeled "Embedding" and includes an icon of a llama and the text "Ollama API." It also mentions "LLMs" (Large Language Models) and points to a "ChromaDB Vectorstore," indicating that the embeddings are stored in a vector database.\n\n4. **ChromaDB Vectorstore**: This stage represents the storage of the embeddings in a vector database. The box is labeled "ChromaDB Vectorstore" and includes the ChromaDB logo, which is a blue and red circle with a yellow center.\n\n5. **Selected LLM**: This stage involves the selection of a specific Large Language Model (LLM) for further processing. The box is labeled "Selected LLM" and points back to the "Embedding" stage, indicating that the selected LLM is used to process the embeddings stored in the vector database.\n\nThe flowchart shows a sequence of steps where content sources are processed through splitting, embedding, and storage in a vector database, and then potentially used by a selected LLM for further analysis or processing. The use of tools like LangChain, Ollama API, and ChromaDB is highlighted to illustrate the technical components involved in this process.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(386.16666666666663), np.float64(466.66666666666663)), (np.float64(386.16666666666663), np.float64(1600.6666666666665)), (np.float64(1486.3333333333333), np.float64(1600.6666666666665)), (np.float64(1486.3333333333333), np.float64(466.66666666666663))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2894, 'layout_height': 4094}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T16:05:13', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 8, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-8-7.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': 'd2b804f0abbe3e656acfa9128292cd56', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-8-7.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-8-7.jpg\nThe image is a flowchart that illustrates the architecture and process of a web application, specifically a Passer Web App, interacting with a local/server-based installation to generate text responses with context. Here\'s a detailed description:\n\n1. **Passer Web App**:\n   - The top left section of the image is labeled "PASSER WEB APP."\n   - Below this label, there is a logo and the text "PRIME REACT," indicating the use of Prime React, a UI library for React.\n\n2. **Prompt + Q + Context**:\n   - Below the "PASSER WEB APP" section, there is a box labeled "Prompt + Q + context."\n   - This box represents the input data that the Passer Web App sends to the local/server-based installation. The "Prompt + Q" is the user\'s query or prompt, and "context" is additional information or context provided to the system.\n\n3. **Local/Server Based Installation**:\n   - The right side of the image is labeled "LOCAL/SERVER BASED INSTALLATION."\n   - Within this section, there is a box labeled "Ollama API," which is the API used to interact with the local/server-based installation.\n   - Below the Ollama API box, there is another box labeled "LLMs," which stands for Large Language Models. This indicates that the system uses large language models to process the input data and generate responses.\n   - At the bottom of the "Local/Server Based Installation" section, there are three gear icons labeled "L," "L," and "M," which likely represent different models or configurations of the language models used.\n\n4. **Generated Text Response with Context**:\n   - At the bottom of the image, there is a box labeled "Generated text response with context."\n   - This box represents the output of the system, which is a text response generated by the language models, incorporating the context provided in the input data.\n\n5. **Flow of Data**:\n   - An arrow points from the "Prompt + Q + context" box on the left to the "Ollama API" box on the right, indicating the flow of data from the Passer Web App to the local/server-based installation.\n   - Another arrow points from the "Ollama API" box to the "Generated text response with context" box, indicating the flow of the generated text response back to the Passer Web App.\n\nThis flowchart effectively illustrates the interaction between the Passer Web App and the local/server-based installation, highlighting the use of Prime React, the Ollama API, and large language models to process prompts and queries with context and generate text responses.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(1536.4999999999998), np