evaluation API**: This is connected to the testing modules and the smart contracts. It appears to be responsible for evaluating the performance of the system using Python.\n\n7. **Smart Contracts**: This component is connected to the Python evaluation API and the Blockchain & IPFS. Smart contracts are typically used in blockchain applications to automate the execution of a contract's terms.\n\n8. **Blockchain & IPFS**: This section is at the bottom right and contains two sub-components: IPFS (InterPlanetary File System) and a blockchain logo. IPFS is connected to the smart contracts and the data pre-processing & vectorization. The blockchain logo is connected to the smart contracts and the data pre-processing & vectorization. This suggests that the system uses blockchain and IPFS for data storage and sharing.\n\n9. **Data Pre-processing & Vectorization**: This component is connected to the LLMs & Vector Database and the Blockchain & IPFS. It likely contains modules for pre-processing and vectorizing data, which is then used by the LLMs & Vector Database and stored in the Blockchain & IPFS.\n\n10. **Login**: This is at the bottom left and appears to be a separate module that is connected to the UI and the web server. It likely handles user authentication and authorization.\n\n11. **WHARF**: This is at the bottom left and appears to be a separate module that is connected to the login. It likely contains some form of authentication or authorization service.\n\nThe flowchart shows the interactions between these components, indicating the sequence of operations and the flow of data within the system. The arrows indicate the direction of data flow and the sequence of operations."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(807.3333333333334), np.float64(1373.1666666666667)), (np.float64(807.3333333333334), np.float64(2175.8333333333335)), (np.float64(2713.6666666666665), np.float64(2175.8333333333335)), (np.float64(2713.6666666666665), np.float64(1373.1666666666667))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2894, 'layout_height': 4094}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T16:05:13', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 21, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-21-11.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': '2c79b3c47ab7ec9639d41b770cd9ab24', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-21-11.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-21-11.jpg\nThe image is a detailed performance comparison chart for a model named "Mistral:7b" across two operating systems: MAC OS and UBUNTU. The chart is divided into two main sections: a horizontal bar chart at the top and a table at the bottom.\n\n### Horizontal Bar Chart:\n- **Title**: "Mistral:7b"\n- **X-Axis**: Represents percentages ranging from 0% to 100%.\n- **Y-Axis**: Lists various metrics for performance evaluation:\n  - Tokens per Second\n  - Total Duration (seconds)\n  - Prompt Evaluation Duration (seconds)\n  - Prompt Evaluation Count\n  - Load Duration Time (seconds)\n  - Evaluation Count (units)\n  - Evaluation Time (seconds)\n- **Legend**: Uses orange for MAC OS and green for UBUNTU.\n- **Metrics**:\n  - **Tokens per Second**: MAC OS shows a higher value than UBUNTU.\n  - **Total Duration (seconds)**: MAC OS has a shorter total duration compared to UBUNTU.\n  - **Prompt Evaluation Duration (seconds)**: MAC OS has a shorter duration than UBUNTU.\n  - **Prompt Evaluation Count**: MAC OS has a higher count than UBUNTU.\n  - **Load Duration Time (seconds)**: MAC OS has a shorter load duration time than UBUNTU.\n  - **Evaluation Count (units)**: MAC OS has a higher evaluation count than UBUNTU.\n  - **Evaluation Time (seconds)**: MAC OS has a shorter evaluation time than UBUNTU.\n\n### Table:\n- **Columns**:\n  - Evaluation Time (seconds)\n  - Evaluation Count (units)\n  - Load Duration Time (seconds)\n  - Prompt Evaluation Count\n  - Prompt Evaluation Duration (seconds)\n  - Total Duration (seconds)\n  - Tokens per Second\n- **Rows**:\n  - MAC OS: 35.864 seconds, 495.86 units, 0.016 seconds, 47.11, 0.557 seconds, 36.440 seconds, 13.91 tokens per second\n  - UBUNTU: 45.325 seconds, 284.31 units, 0.039 seconds, 53.81, 4.488 seconds, 49.856 seconds, 6.36 tokens per second\n\n### Summary:\nThe chart and table show that MAC OS outperforms UBUNTU in terms of most metrics, including tokens per second, total duration, prompt evaluation duration, and evaluation count. However, UBUNTU has a longer load duration time and a longer evaluation time. The evaluation count is higher on MAC OS, indicating more evaluations were performed.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(807.3333333333334), np.float64(2625.0)), (np.float64(807.3333333333334), np.float64(3425.333333333333)), (np.float64(2730.0), np.float64(3425.333333333333)), (np.float64(2730.0), np.float64(2625.0))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2894, 'layout_height': 4094}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T16:05:13', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 21, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-21-12.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_44c3d19297fec5dad77b32cba42d667a.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': '8af45387e4cbf1d5d8a6cc53be9c5fd2', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-21-12.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-21-12.jpg\nThe image is a bar chart comparing the performance metrics of Llama2:7b on two different operating systems: MAC OS and UBUNTU. The chart is divided into two sections, each representing the performance metrics for the respective operating system. The metrics are as follows:\n\n1. **Tokens per Second**: This metric is represented by the length of the bars. The MAC OS bar is longer than the UBUNTU bar, indicating a higher number of tokens processed per second on MAC OS.\n\n2. **Total Duration (seconds)**: This metric is also represented by the length of the bars. The MAC OS bar is shorter than the UBUNTU bar, indicating a shorter total duration on MAC OS.\n\n3. **Prompt Evaluation Duration (seconds)**: This metric is represented by the length of the bars. The MAC OS bar is shorter than the UBUNTU bar, indicating a shorter duration for prompt evaluation on MAC OS.\n\n4. **Prompt Evaluation Count**: This metric is represented by the length of the bars. The MAC OS bar is longer than the UBUNTU bar, indicating a higher count of prompt evaluations on MAC OS.\n\n5. **Load Duration Time (seconds)**: This metric is represented by the length of the bars. The MAC OS bar is shorter than the UBUNTU bar, indicating a shorter duration for loading on MAC OS.\n\n6. **Evaluation Count (units)**: This metric is represented by the length of the bars. The MAC OS bar is longer than the UBUNTU bar, indicating a higher count of evaluations on MAC OS.\n\n7. **Evaluation Time (seconds)**: This metric is represented by the length of the bars. The MAC OS bar is shorter than the UBUNTU bar, indicating a shorter duration for evaluation on MAC OS.\n\nBelow the bar chart, there is a table with the following columns:\n\n- **Evaluation Time (seconds)**: The time taken for evaluation in seconds.\n- **Evaluation Count (units)**: The number